-- check/bad: §6.3.1 step 4's exclusion, seen from the USE.
--
-- A type any of whose constructor payloads contains a function type gets
-- neither derived method (A.23), so the eager pass emits nothing for
-- `Handler` — and a use has to agree with that pass exactly, or `<` would
-- name a function nobody wrote. `eq` keeps `not_equatable`, which §3.4
-- says is the better message; `compare` has no marker of its own and says
-- what it found instead.
pub type Handler
    = Handler (Int -> Int)


pub before : Handler, Handler -> Bool
before a b = a < b


pub same : Handler, Handler -> Bool
same a b = a == b
